### Enable foreign keys with PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON

Source: https://www.sqlite.org/foreignkeys.html

Use this command to enable foreign key constraints for the current database connection. Foreign keys are disabled by default for backwards compatibility, so this must be run for each connection. The command is a no-op if the library is compiled with SQLITE_OMIT_TRIGGER but not SQLITE_OMIT_FOREIGN_KEY.

```sql
sqlite> PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
```

--------------------------------

### Check and toggle foreign_keys with PRAGMA foreign_keys

Source: https://www.sqlite.org/foreignkeys.html

This command-line session shows how to query the current foreign key setting and toggle it ON/OFF. The PRAGMA returns 0 when disabled and 1 when enabled. If it returns no data, the SQLite version does not support foreign keys (older than 3.6.19 or compiled with SQLITE_OMIT_FOREIGN_KEY or SQLITE_OMIT_TRIGGER).

```sql
sqlite> PRAGMA foreign_keys;
0
sqlite> PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
sqlite> PRAGMA foreign_keys;
1
sqlite> PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;
sqlite> PRAGMA foreign_keys;
0
```
